abstract: >-
  Educational software for studying the implementation of rural heart failure
  workflows. Version 1.11.0 adds confirmed medication schedules by local day,
  versioned ten-input risk assessments, scoped alert reconciliation, explicit
  portal message read receipts and reconciled reports and exports. An
  account-free sandbox lets visitors follow a fictional case from a simulated
  alert to a documented human decision. The interface uses the typography and
  colors of the HEARTLAND site, with keyboard navigation, enlarged chart
  readings and high-contrast form controls. Bilingual language assistance and
  reviewed synthetic audio accompany deterministic rules and human review.
  The app supports synthetic demonstration and controlled evaluation. Clinical
  validation and prospective patient outcomes require separate evidence.
keywords:
  - heart failure
